# How to Implement the Dynamic Dropdown custom-component in Kissflow

1. Download the index.html file.

2. Upload as a Custom Component
    1. Compress the file into a ZIP archive.
    2. Upload it as a custom component in your Kissflow app.

3. Create Required Variables (Case-sensitive)
    1. DropdownValues: A variable storing drop-down options as a comma-separated list (e.g., "Option1, Option2, Option3").
    2. SelectedValue: A variable that will store the user-selected value from the dropdown.
🚨 Important: Variable names are case-sensitive, so ensure they are entered exactly as specified.

    Use Case Example:
        1. If filtering a performance report by department, update DropdownValues with department names (e.g., "Sales, Marketing, HR").
        2. Create a filter parameter in the report and link it to SelectedValue to dynamically display relevant data.

4. Add the Component to a Page
    1. Insert the custom component into your page.
    2. Adjust its size and alignment to match your app’s style.

5. Functionality Notes
    The "All" option is included by default. Selecting it resets the filter, displaying unfiltered data.


It’s Done!

Your dynamic dropdown is now fully implemented.
